# Task 162-024 Execution Plan

## Goal
READ-ONLY audit of `src/cli/commands/` lifecycle commands:
- start.ts, status.ts, kill.ts, cleanup.ts, checkpoint.ts, run.ts

## Lead Questions
1. ADR-022-V2 CLI/MCP parity — do MCP tool parameters mirror CLI flags?
2. --dry-run consistency — same semantics across commands?
3. kill confirmation — destructive action guard rails?

## 10 Audit Dimensions
1. Dead code (unused exports / params)
2. ADR violations (ADR-010 single dep, ADR-022-V2 parity, ADR-025 graceful shutdown,
   ADR-037 RBAC kill scope)
3. Conflicting areas (duplicate logic across lifecycle commands)
4. Drift (help text vs behavior, claims vs reality)
5. Type safety (any, ts-ignore, as unknown as)
6. Dependency hygiene (.js extensions, circular deps)
7. Documentation pollution (orphan/outdated)
8. Memory V2 coherence (where applicable)
9. Config integrity (--root, --json, --dry-run uniform handling)
10. Migration triage classification

## Steps
1. Read all 6 lifecycle command files
2. Read MCP tool counterparts (start, status, kill, cleanup, checkpoint, run)
3. Compare CLI flags ↔ MCP zod schemas for parity
4. Find boundary violations / dead code / drift
5. Write single audit report to docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-024-cli-lifecycle.md
6. Write result file

## Constraints
- READ-ONLY: do NOT modify any src/* file
- scope.filesWrite single path: docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-024-cli-lifecycle.md
- ADR-037 RBAC enforced
